# Public site UI

Read `docs/UI_PUBLIC_GUIDELINES.md` before changing these files. Key rules:

- Positioning: website review with issue evidence. Issues go Open → In progress → Ready for verification → Verified → Closed. Video is evidence on an issue, never a separate product.
- No invented proof (quotes, logos, numbers) and no claims about unshipped features.
- Prices, limits, and trial length come only from `src/lib/billing/plans.ts`.
- Page rhythm: `.hero-backdrop` hero with one `h1` → sections using `SectionIntro` → `SiteCta`.
- Auth links use `authRoutes` from `src/lib/site.ts`.
- Cards: `rounded-2xl bg-card ring-1 ring-foreground/10`. Controls use `border-input`; `border-border` is decorative only.
- Use tokens (`bg-surface`, `bg-brand-dark`, `text-brand-dark-accent`, …), never raw hex.
- No horizontal scroll at 320–1440 px. Stretched card links need a visible `has-[a:focus-visible]` outline.
